{
  "id": "shifan_luogu",
  "name": "Shifan luogu (Wuxi-Suzhou gong-drum and wind ensemble)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Ensemble music of southern Jiangsu, centred on Wuxi and Suzhou and part of the wider sunan chuida family; pieces alternate and combine passages for winds and strings (dizi, sheng, erhu, pipa, sanxian) with elaborate passages for drums, gongs and cymbals, while the related shifan gu foregrounds the drum without gongs. Long played by Daoist musicians and amateur clubs for rites and festivities, it was transcribed and studied by the Wuxi-born musicologist Yang Yinliu and is listed as national intangible heritage.",
  "recipe": "classic modern shifan luogu, groove Percussion, east Asian branch. bitter bamboo phyllostachys nigra canonical jiangnan suzhou qudi southern jiangnan kunqu canonical lyrical dizi, sheng, bamboo stick horsehair threaded between strings erhu, pipa, danpigu, gong chau gong tamtam, naobo. field recording. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
